{
  "category": "Trash Heap Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "It clenches opponents with its left arm and finishes them off with foul-smelling poison gas belched from its mouth.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "They absorb garbage and make it part of their bodies. They shoot a poisonous liquid from their right-hand fingertips.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "Consuming garbage makes new kinds of poison gases and liquids inside their bodies.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Consuming garbage makes new kinds of poison gases and liquids inside their bodies.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It clenches opponents with its left arm and finishes them off with foul-smelling poison gas belched from its mouth.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "Consuming garbage makes new kinds of poison gases and liquids inside their bodies.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "It clenches opponents with its left arm and finishes them off with foul-smelling poison gas belched from its mouth.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Consuming garbage makes new kinds of poison gases and liquids inside their bodies.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Beware the poisonous liquid it shoots from its right arm. If even a little of it gets on you, you’ll experience the effects of the unidentified toxin.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "For a time, their numbers increased explosively in Alola. Since the arrival of Grimer, their population has decreased dramatically.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It locks opponents in place with its left hand, immobilizing them by entirely dousing their bodies with poisonous liquid.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Some say the reason Garbodor in Alola are a little stronger than their counterparts elsewhere is the presence of Muk, their natural enemy.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon eats trash, which turns into poison inside its body. The main component of the poison depends on what sort of trash was eaten.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "The toxic liquid it launches from its right arm is so virulent that it can kill a weakened creature instantly.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
